@startuml
' Derived from tests/test_cli.py:747-810 (the ast import guard's rank table) and
' src/nonogram/__init__.py. NOT from the C4 diagram: the ranks are what the test
' enforces, and the test is the authority on what the code may do.
title ADR-0007 dependency ranks — an import must reach a STRICTLY deeper rank

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "rank 0 — adapters  (_ADAPTERS, tests/test_cli.py:747)" {
  [COMP-001 cli.py] as CLI
  [COMP-008 web/] as WEB
  [COMP-009 admin/] as ADMIN
}

package "rank 1 — orchestrator" {
  [COMP-002 orchestrator.py] as ORCH
  [nonogram/__init__.py] as ROOT
}

package "rank 2 — capabilities (discovered from disk, not listed)" {
  [COMP-003 sourcing/] as SRC
  [COMP-004 clues.py] as CLUES
  [COMP-005 solver/] as SOLVER
  [COMP-006 difficulty.py] as DIFF
  [COMP-007 export/] as EXPORT
  [COMP-010 db/] as DB
  [analysis/  (no COMP id)] as ANALYSIS
}

package "rank 3 — shared (_SHARED, tests/test_cli.py:749)" {
  [errors.py] as ERRORS
  [limits.py] as LIMITS
}

CLI --> ORCH
WEB --> ORCH
ADMIN --> ORCH

ORCH --> SRC
ORCH --> CLUES
ORCH --> SOLVER
ORCH --> DIFF
ORCH --> EXPORT

' Legal because admin/ is rank 0: ADR-0032/R1's storage guard re-derives clues
' and asks the solver for a verdict AT the storage boundary, rather than
' trusting whoever called it. Routing them through COMP-002 would erase that.
ADMIN --> CLUES
ADMIN --> SOLVER
ADMIN --> DIFF
ADMIN --> EXPORT
ADMIN --> SRC
ADMIN --> DB

SRC ..> ERRORS
SOLVER ..> ERRORS
EXPORT ..> LIMITS
ORCH ..> ERRORS

' The single directed exemption: _LAUNCH_EDGE = ("cli", "web"),
' tests/test_cli.py:760. ADR-0008 keeps one console entry point, so
' `nonogram serve` lives in cli.py's argparse tree. The reverse is a violation.
CLI -[#blue]-> WEB : _LAUNCH_EDGE\n(the only same-rank import)

note right of SOLVER
  The absence of arrows BETWEEN rank-2 boxes
  is the architecture, not an omission:
  2 <= 2 fails the guard's comparison
  (tests/test_cli.py:885).

  Hence solver/propagate.py:403 `mask_runs`
  reimplements clues.encode_line natively and
  is cross-checked from the test tree instead.
end note

note bottom
  Enforced by an ast walk over src/nonogram/**/*.py,
  not by a linter and not by convention:
  tests/test_cli.py :: test_every_import_in_the_package_points_inward
end note

@enduml
